# Phase-4 replay archive — drop idempotency: a duplicated drop report (Steam
# reliable retransmission style, injected with the dup fault) must NOT
# re-broadcast — the receivers would materialize AND re-place the same item.
# G2 sees exactly one ItemDrop frame.
#
# Mechanism: FireItemDroppedReceived's duplicate guard — same itemId + same
#            position + same rotation = silent (ItemService.cs:372-375)
# Observed once live: "not present — materializing" followed by
# "present — re-placing" for one drop (the bug this guard fixed).
# Known boundary (recorded 2026-08-12): the guard cannot distinguish a
# retransmission from a genuine re-drop at the SAME spot — a pick-drop-pick
# at one exact position would be swallowed. The replay injection drops at
# (10,10) (ItemSimWorld.Drop) so the first drop never collides with the
# spawn spot (0,0).

@0 spawn g1 42 test_item 1.0
@33 expect host_table 42 within 500
@33 fault g1 host dup
@33 drop g1 42 test_item 1.0
@66 expect host_table 42 within 500
@66 expect received g2 ItemDrop 1
